":0.3203212311319955,"imag_component_TV_from_full_orbital":0.3203212311319955,"two_real_mixture_max_probability_residual":2.7755575615628914e-17,"spectral_vs_literal_amplitude_sup_residual":1.4304896245381992e-15},{"center_mode":-15,"cycles":6,"complex_positive_band_velocity_cells_per_cycle":-0.5999866638261535,"opposite_band_negative_momentum_velocity":-0.5999866638261535,"real_component_TV_from_full_orbital":0.3184393700829836,"imag_component_TV_from_full_orbital":0.31843937008298373,"two_real_mixture_max_probability_residual":2.0816681711721685e-17,"spectral_vs_literal_amplitude_sup_residual":1.965949188660863e-15}],"real_source_scope":"On a chain let D multiply a configuration by i^(number on odd sites). In D-dagger coordinates both alternating nearest bond matrices in left-to-right basis are [[c,s],[-s,c]] (s=4/5 or 3/5). Vacuum, local double occupation and all real diagonal readouts retain their rules. A sharply occupied launch changes only by a global phase. If psi in this chart is x+i y, every native terminal or adaptive occupation-read history has real Kraus matrix K and probability ||Kx||^2+||Ky||^2. Preparing x or y normalized with probabilities ||x||^2 and ||y||^2 for a normalized psi reproduces all those records. This is a classical mixture of real coherent states, not an assertion of efficient preparation or of agreement on arbitrary independently held phase-sensitive analyzers. A component could be zero for general psi; remove it from the mixture.","real_ray_scope":"For a scalar positive-band state in a gapped symmetric chart, complex conjugation in the real coordinate gauge changes k to -k and e^(-i omega(k)) to e^(+i omega(-k)). The conjugate sector is orthogonal and both components of the complex orbital have equal norm 1/sqrt(2), including a many-body state in the exterior product of that band. Eigenphase odd-sign reversal and k reversal give identical group velocity. Each normalized real component puts at most twice the full positive-band probability outside any event, so either inherits weak concentration of the ordered rays. The mixture retains all occupation probabilities even for non-concentrated quantum states; a single real component can have different finite interference fringes. A generally fully localized site cannot be assumed to have prepared a narrow one-band packet. The illustrative periodic single-particle mode packets test real recurrent propagation, not convergence rates or the preparation of an arbitrary orbital from a single launch.","basis":"Increasing mode labels on an open chain 0..N-1. A binary occupation has no repeated site. Even bonds (0,1),(2,3),... precede odd bonds (1,2),(3,4),...; uncovered end modes are untouched. Pairs (u,v) in the integer data mean u+iv. Divide each amplitude by the stated history denominator times sqrt(initial squared norm).","law":"Each two-mode gate has vacuum numerator 5, one-occupant block 3I-4iX or 4I+3iX, and doubly-occupied numerator 5*contact_sign, all over 5. One-body blocks have determinant +1. For contact_sign=+1 the full evolution is the exterior power, independently checked from determinants of chronological one-body products. For sign=-1 each active bond contributes a controlled occupation phase on |11>; disjoint bonds commute and one-body behavior is identical. Both laws preserve exclusion and norm. Overall conjugation of all gates AND launch data preserves every coordinate probability; reverse time uses the conjugate-transpose gates in inverse layer order.","minimality":"Within each layer the two laws differ by a diagonal product of signs on the doubly occupied disjoint bonds. This phase commutes with that layer. It leaves its own coordinate measurement unchanged for every coherent input. On a localized input the initial layer's sign is also global. Thus no one-layer terminal coordinate distinguishes arbitrary inputs, or two-layer terminal coordinate distinguishes localized inputs for any chain length. In the two-mode two-particle space the dimension is one. Three open modes attain both bounds; one-body sectors never distinguish. Terminal coordinate records made after intermediate full occupation reads must sum incoherently across the recorded histories.","evidence_scope":"Four-mode Pluecker control detects genuine departure from the manifold of single two-fermion Slater states. It is stronger than a port difference on three modes, where any pure two-fermion vector is decomposable. Both finite laws are local occupation rules; these examples alone imply neither a unique exchange principle nor a continuum interaction, scattering strength, or statistics of other particles.","port_columns":["occupied_sites","determinant_lift_numerator","minus_contact_numerator","determinant_probability","minus_contact_probability"],"census":[{"N":2,"particles":1,"source":"localized","input_count":2,"relative_phases":null,"number_of_inputs_with_a_coordinate_difference_by_time":[0,0,0,0,0],"first_time_with_positive_coordinate_difference":null},{"N":2,"particles":1,"source":"two_coordinate_superposition","input_count":3,"relative_phases":[[1,0],[-1,0],[0,1]],"number_of_inputs_with_a_coordinate_difference_by_time":[0,0,0,0,0],"first_time_with_positive_coordinate_difference":null},{"N":2,"particles":2,"source":"localized","input_count":1,"relative_phases":null,"number_of_inputs_with_a_coordinate_difference_by_time":[0,0,0,0,0],"first_time_with_positive_coordinate_difference":null},{"N":2,"particles":2,"source":"two_coordinate_superposition","input_count":0,"relative_phases":[[1,0],[-1,0],[0,1]],"number_of_inputs_with_a_coordinate_difference_by_time":[0,0,0,0,0],"first_time_with_positive_coordinate_difference":null},{"N":3,"particles":1,"source":"localized","input_count":3,"relative_phases":null,"number_of_inputs_with_a_coordinate_difference_by_time":[0,0,0,0,0],"first_time_with_positive_coordinate_difference":null},{"N":3,"particles":1,"source":"two_coordinate_superposition","input_count":9,"relative_phases":[[1,0],[-1,0],[0,1]]